      "textEn": "116\n\nPronunciation, procedure, sacrificer, priest, sacrifice-fruit, sacrifice-shala, time of sacrifice, etc., are different.\nThey are not. Mandhata, knowing the rules of self-realization, worshiped the Supreme Being, who is situated on a divine position,\nwho is the form of God Vishnu, who is endowed with all the gods. He also gave abundant donations to the Brahmins,\nand in this way, he performed a Yagya (ritual) to worship God. As long as the sun rises, as long as it shines. That whole field is called the Yauvanashva's field. 37. Meaning of the word\n\nYavat—Until; Suryah—Sun; Udayiti—rises; Sm—in the past tense; Yavat—Until; Cha—also; Pratitishthati—remains; Tat—\nThe above mentioned objects; Sarvam—All; Yauvanashwasya—son of Yauvanashwa; Mandhatah—of Mandhata; Kshetram—place; Uchyate—is called. In the horizon, from where the sun rises and shines, and where the sun sets, all those places\nare considered under the authority of the famous Mandhata, the son of Yuwanashva. Shashabinduhitari Bindumatyaadhanya rapah.\nPurukutsamabarisham Muchukundam cha yoginam. They were all happy, and fifty-five hundred were married. 38. Meaning of the word\n\nShashabindoah—of Shashabindu Raja; Duhitari—daughter; Bindumatyam—from Bindumati; Adhat—produced; Nripah—by the king (Mandhata);\nPurukutsam—to Purukuts; Ambarisham—to Ambarisha; Muchukundam—to Muchukunda; Cha—and; Yoginam—yogi; Tesham—from them;\nSwasarah—sisters; Panchasat—fifty; Saubharim—to Saubharishi; Vabhiri—accepted; Patim—in the form of husband..\nFrom the womb of Bindumati, the daughter of Shashabindu, three sons were born to Mandhata. Their names were Purukuts,\nAmbarisha and the great Yogi Muchukunda. These three brothers had fifty sisters who chose Saubhari Rishi as their husband. He who is immersed in the water of Yamuna, is absorbed in penance. Having seen the sight of the king's enjoyment, the lustful ones. 39). Jatasuhiro Nripam Vipraah Kanyamekamayachata.\nMay I take you to the Grihya Sutra